<cell>
<cname>fir</cname>
<text>This cell contains an example of a so-called finite impulse response filter.   Evaluate this cell to compute and show the result of applying this fir filter to the input signal defined in the text field of cell >INPUT.</text>
<val>1.00</val>
<script>set tap1 to 0
set tap2 to 0
set tap3 to 0
out("\nFIR Filter Example")
out("\ninput signal, output signal")
while(not  eof) {
     in(INPUT)
     set tap3 to tap2
     set tap2 to tap1
     set tap1 to INPUT
     set fir to tap1/4+tap2/2+tap3/4  
     out("\n",INPUT,",",fir)
}</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>home</cname>
<text>The cell called >iir contains a script that performs a so-called infinite impulse response filter operation on the input defined in the cell called INPUT.

The cell called >fir contains a script which performs a so-called finite impulse response filter operation on the input defined in the cell called INPUT.
</text></cell>
<cell>
<cname>iir</cname>
<text>This cell contains an example of a so-called infinite impulse response filter.  This is the simplest possible such filter.
Evaluate this cell to compute and show the result of applying this iir filter to the input signal defined in the text field of cell >INPUT.</text>
<val>0.76</val>
<script>set iir to 0
while(not eof) {
     set index to index+1
     in(INPUT)
     set iir to (iir+INPUT)/2
     out("\n",INPUT,",",iir)
}</script></cell>
